# What the sdist carries.
#
# **The test suite is shipped, so it has to be shippable.** Without this file the sdist held
# `test/test_ichiwatashi.py` and nothing else from that directory: no `__init__.py`, so
# `python -m unittest discover -s test -t .` failed there with "Start directory is not importable", and no
# `data/`, so the one fixture the colour-difference test reads was missing. A file that looks like a test
# suite and cannot run is the same shape as a wheel that looked installed and could not find its font.
include LICENSE
include README.md
recursive-include test *.py
recursive-include test/data *
